    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "A curve is defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=-3{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),\\,y=2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t),\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nDetermine the values of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is horizontal. Give exact answers.\n\nIn **ascending order**, the tangent to the curve is horizontal at $t=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $t=$\n{{field-2}}.",
